      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence if the first term is $-5$ and the common difference is $-1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the first term is $f(1)=-5$ and the common difference is $d=-1.$ So, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-5+(n-1)(-1) \\\\  & =-5-n+1 \\\\  & =-4-n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is $f(n)=-4-n.$",
