      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the $25$th term of the following arithmetic sequence. \n\n$$\n4,\\,8,\\,12,\\,16,\\,…\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nFirst, we will write the formula for the $n$th term of this sequence. From the first few terms\n\n$$\n4,\\,8,\\,12,\\,16,\\,…,\n$$\n\nwe see that the first term is ${a}_{1}=4$ and the common difference is \n\n$$\nd=8-4=4.\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =4+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =4+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use our formula to find the $25$th term. All we have to do is substitute $n=25:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =4n \\\\ {a}_{25} & =4(25) \\\\  & =100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $25$th term of the sequence is ${a}_{25}=100.$",
